# Strata TODO

Sorted easiest first. Tags: [config] = flag or setting only, no code. [ui] = web app only.
[py] = serve/server.py. [eng] = C++ engine. [exists] = already works, just not obvious.
Renamed 2026-10-24: items have short names instead of numbers. The numbers had outlived
their usefulness - four sessions renumbered the file, each pass invalidating cross-references
and the `todo #N` comments in the code, and twice a scripted renumber corrupted the file on the
way. A name cannot collide with a neighbour, so there is nothing to keep in sequence.

NAMING. Each item's line starts with its name in backticks, e.g. `pin-conversation`. Code
comments cite it as `todo #pin-conversation`; prose in this file says "item pin-conversation".
Names are lowercase, hyphenated, and describe the want rather than the symptom. To find an item from a code comment: grep -n '`pin-conversation`' todo. To find the code from an item: grep -rn 'todo #pin-conversation' serve/.
Adding an item: pick a name no other line uses; do not extend a sequence.

LINE REFERENCES rot. Items cite code as `file:line`, and 80 of them in this file are already
as-of their writing date; a session that edits the code invalidates them silently. When you pick
up an item, re-find the cited code by symbol before trusting the number, and write new
references as `function_name in serve/server.py` rather than `serve/server.py:4001` where the
number is not essential.

HISTORICAL NAMES. Work done and removed from this file on 2026-10-23 is still cited by code
comments, and those comments used to point at bare numbers that named nothing. They now name the
work: leave-warning (513721b8), start-beep (ae1598b0), keep-thinking-open, keep-tool-calls-open
and tool-click-open (all three 78d2a8d1), update-in-place (19aca0c2), md-per-author and md-button
(86c61adb, 3ebbb7fe). keep-thinking-open and keep-tool-calls-open no longer exist as switches at
all: fold-control replaced them, and the four overlapping switches became one control.

