    THE DOT'S MEANING CHANGED, and this is the part worth keeping: it is NOT "this chat differs from the
    defaults". Editing this chat's own list never raises it. It means the CONFIG moved under the chat: the chat
    remembers what it was synced to (c.mcpDefault), and the dot is (chat list != current) AND (the baseline !=
    current). setChatTools re-syncs the baseline, which is why an edit here leaves the dot dark.
    Control that proves it: dropping the baseline re-sync fails only in the case where the chat ends up different
    from the settings on purpose - the first version of the test unticked a tool until the chat matched the
